      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: I tried to upload the same avatar with a new upload code several times. I also tried to see if it was also happening when I used VRChat on a different PC. It had the same outcome as above. I had to reset my avatar on the VRChat website every time, because if I tried to login while still on that avatar, the game would do this weird thing immediately when my home world load. There was no possibility for me to use the menu ingame when I tried to change into the new avatar!! It was not possible to click anything, it did not show me where I was clicking nor did it react to anything I tried. So in the end for now I just deleted the avatar from my uploads again. Another thing might also be possible, that the clothing file I used, which I put on my avatar via Blender, might be corrupted. But in Unity and Blender both it looked fine. So I have no idea...",
      "viewerReactions": null,
